# GC Meet Helper — Calendar PR review (`y-agt-gc-meet-helper`)

Use when the user asks to **prepare a PR review meeting**, **Google Calendar meeting text**, **calendar title/description for a PR**, or similar — especially after a PR exists or during the Task PR flow ([`y-git-create-pr.mdc`](../git/y-git-create-pr.mdc) step 16).

---

## Step 0 — Mode (mandatory first step)

Before PR discovery, drafting, or any Calendar work, use **`AskQuestion`**:

| Option | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| **Generate title and description only** | Agent drafts title + styled description; **user** creates the event manually and copy-pastes. **Default** when the user did not say “create the event”. |
| **Create draft event in Google Calendar** | After draft approval, agent creates a **draft** event on the user’s calendar via **Google Calendar MCP** (see [Google Calendar connection](#google-calendar-connection-required-for-create-path)). |
| **`other`** | User explains a variant. |

**Rules:**

- **Do not** discover PRs, draft text, or call Calendar APIs until step 0 is answered — **unless** the user **already stated the mode** in the same message.
- If the user chose **Generate title and description only**, **do not** create or update Calendar events in that run.
- If the user chose **Create draft event**, follow [Path B](#path-b--create-draft-event-in-google-calendar) and **do not** fall back to silent manual-only unless MCP auth fails after the user is prompted to connect.

---

## Google Calendar connection (required for create path)

Creating events requires **OAuth** to the user’s Google account via the **local Calendar MCP** at **`~/.calendar-mcp/mcp-google-calendar`**.

### Local MCP (preferred)

| Item | Path |
|------|------|
| **MCP server** | `~/.calendar-mcp/mcp-google-calendar/index.js` |
| **Cursor launcher** | `~/.cursor/scripts/run-mcp-google-calendar.sh` |
| **Env file** | `~/.cursor/google-calendar-mcp.env` (copy from `google-calendar-mcp.env.example`) |
| **Tokens** | `~/.calendar-mcp/credentials.json` (from `npm run auth`) |
| **One-shot draft script** | `cd ~/.calendar-mcp/mcp-google-calendar && npm run create-draft` |

**`~/.cursor/mcp.json`** should point `google-calendar` at **`run-mcp-google-calendar.sh`**, not `npx @gongrzhe/...`.

### First-time OAuth (user or agent runs once)

1. Google Cloud Console → enable **Google Calendar API** → **OAuth Desktop** client → copy Client ID + Secret.
2. Create **`~/.cursor/google-calendar-mcp.env`** with `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`, optional `GOOGLE_TIMEZONE=Asia/Dubai`.
3. Run:
   ```bash
   cd ~/.calendar-mcp/mcp-google-calendar && npm install && npm run auth
   ```
4. Open the printed URL, authorize, paste the code. Tokens save to **`~/.calendar-mcp/credentials.json`**.
5. **Reload Cursor MCP** (Settings → MCP → `google-calendar` green).

### Before the first create in a session

1. **Detect MCP** — `google-calendar` / `create_event` in available tools, **or** local env + credentials exist.
2. **If MCP tool unavailable but local setup is ready** — run **`npm run create-draft`** in `~/.calendar-mcp/mcp-google-calendar` with approved title/description (update `create-draft-event.mjs` or pass env vars for this run).
3. **If auth missing** — stop create path; run **`npm run auth`** or fix env; do not guess credentials.
4. **Do not** create events until API call succeeds or user confirms OAuth is complete.

**Handoff when blocked:** offer **Generate title and description only** with the same draft content.

---

## Draft event (create path — required behavior)

When the user chose **Create draft event in Google Calendar**, create a **draft shell** the user finishes in the Calendar UI.

| Field | Rule |
|--------|------|
| **Duration** | **15 minutes** by default. Override only when the user specifies another length in chat or **`AskQuestion`**. |
| **Start** | **Current date and time** in the **user’s local timezone** (from user info, system, or ask once). **Round to the next minute** if the MCP requires whole minutes. |
| **End** | Start + duration. |
| **Overlaps** | **Do not** check free/busy, suggest slots, or move the start time to avoid conflicts. **Always use “now”** even if it overlaps existing events. |
| **Attendees** | **None** on create. **Do not** invite reviewers, resolve emails, or send updates. User adds guests later. |
| **Google Meet / conference** | **Do not** add unless the user explicitly asks in this run. |
| **Notifications** | **Do not** send invite emails (`sendUpdates: none` or MCP equivalent). |
| **Status** | Use **`tentative`** when the MCP/API supports it; otherwise default event status on primary calendar. |
| **Calendar** | User’s **primary** calendar unless they name another. |
| **Summary** | Approved **title** (see [Title format](#title-format-required)). |
| **Description** | API-safe **plain text** from the approved draft (strip `**`; keep URLs and line breaks). |

After create, return the **event link** (`htmlLink` or MCP equivalent), **start**, **end**, **timezone**, and remind the user they can **change time, add guests, add Meet**, and edit any field in Google Calendar.

