## Title format (required)

Plain text (Calendar **Summary**). Output in a **`text`** fenced code block for generate-only; use the same string for API **summary**.

### Single PR

```text
PR Review - <JIRA-KEY>#<pr-number>
```

Example: `PR Review - VAP-2668#807`

### Multiple PRs

```text
PRs Review - <JIRA-KEY-1>#<pr-number-1> <JIRA-KEY-2>#<pr-number-2> …
```

Example: `PRs Review - VAP-3159#918 VAP-3151#919`

### Title rules

- Prefix: **`PR Review -`** (one PR) or **`PRs Review -`** (multiple).
- Pairs: **`<JIRA-KEY>#<pr-number>`** — no space before `#`; space between pairs.
- Ascending Jira key order unless the user asks otherwise.
- No repo name or URLs in the title.

---

## Description format (required) — copy from styled chat

Google Calendar **Description** (manual paste):

- **Does not** render pasted **HTML** or Markdown from a **code block**.
- **Does** keep **rich text** when the user copies **rendered** Markdown from the chat (bold, bullets, links).

### Agent output (styled Markdown — not a code block)

Under **`### Description (copy from here)`**, write **normal Markdown in the message body**. **Never** fence the description.

**One bullet (`-`) per Jira task**, same order as the title:

1. **Bold headline:** `**VAP-xxxx — &lt;short headline&gt;**`
2. Blank line → summary (1–3 sentences, outcome-focused).
3. Blank line → **`**Task:** https://vendoroo-dev.atlassian.net/browse/VAP-xxxx`**
4. Blank line → **`**PR:** https://github.com/.../pull/&lt;n&gt;`**

Use **full URLs** (not `[label](url)`). **No HTML tags.**

**Generate-only handoff:** *Select the **Description** section below, copy, paste into Calendar Description.*

**Create path — API description:** convert approved draft to plain text, e.g.:

```text
VAP-3159 — Filter non-resident AIResidentCom at debounce dispatch until ROY-191
Persists all valid AIResidentCom updates in message_buffer, then marks non-resident Todo rows Skipped at debounce dispatch so ResiRoo only processes resident-eligible messages when RESIROO_MULTI_ROLE_MESSAGES_ENABLED=false (default).
Task: https://vendoroo-dev.atlassian.net/browse/VAP-3159
PR: https://github.com/Vendoroo/generative-search/pull/918

VAP-3151 — Limit Generative Search Number of Images to get Processed to a maximum of 5
Adds RESIROO_MAX_IMAGES_TO_ANALYZE (default 5) and caps inbound ImageUrls at the start of image analysis, so vision analysis, DB storage, attachment metadata, and outbound ImageAnalysis all use the first five images per resident turn.
Task: https://vendoroo-dev.atlassian.net/browse/VAP-3151
PR: https://github.com/Vendoroo/generative-search/pull/919
```

